/T (We used Figma to create our medium-fidelity prototype, along with ChatGPT and Notability to brainstorm ideas and create rough sketches during our early design process.)
/E (We used Figma to create our medium-fidelity prototype, along with ChatGPT and Notability to brainstorm ideas and create rough sketches during our early design process.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
504 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 314 0 R
/T (Pros: Figma allowed us to create a consistent design system, build reusable interface elements, and connect screens into interactive user flows. One of its biggest advantages was how easy it became to wire interactions together once our screens were designed.)
/E (Pros: Figma allowed us to create a consistent design system, build reusable interface elements, and connect screens into interactive user flows. One of its biggest advantages was how easy it became to wire interactions together once our screens were designed.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
505 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 314 0 R
/T (Cons: However, we underestimated how much time it would take to build everything in Figma. Creating and refining individual screens was significantly slower than we expected. We also encountered some unexpected alignment issues with our buttons, which we later corrected based on feedback.)
/E (Cons: However, we underestimated how much time it would take to build everything in Figma. Creating and refining individual screens was significantly slower than we expected. We also encountered some unexpected alignment issues with our buttons, which we later corrected based on feedback.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
