513 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 316 0 R
/T (Limitations of the prototype: What was left out? Why?)
/E (Limitations of the prototype: What was left out? Why?)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
514 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 920 0 R
/E (One of our biggest limitations is that we have not yet built the physical duck, which is a central part of our product concept. Our medium-fidelity prototype therefore focuses primarily on the digital experience.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
515 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 921 0 R
/E (We also chose not to implement every possible user flow. For example, we left out optional features such as connecting Google Calendar and expanding contact selection. Instead, we focused on a smaller set of representative interactions that communicate the core functionality of our product.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
516 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 316 0 R
/E (We made this decision because we wanted users to understand and evaluate the main experience without being overwhelmed by additional features. These flows are still important to our long-term vision, but they were not essential to testing our current design.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
517 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 922 0 R
/E (App selection, contact selection, and focus duration: These interactions use predefined options and outcomes rather than storing or processing real user preferences.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
518 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 923 0 R
/E ( Statistics: All displayed statistics are hard-coded examples. They do not reflect actual user behavior or tracked focus sessions.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
519 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 924 0 R
/E (External integrations: Features such as Google Calendar connectivity are not implemented.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
520 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 925 0 R
/E (Physical duck \(Wizard of Oz\): The duck isn't built yet, so a facilitator acts it out: telling users when it would glow, quack or droop, and switching Home between the Healthy, Okay and Sick screens to show its health changing.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
521 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 317 0 R
/E (Other Wizard of Oz: duck pairing is faked \(the Bluetooth search always "finds" the duck\), and the facilitator tells users when an app would be blocked. These simulations let us show the final experience without building the underlying systems.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
