/P 927 0 R
/E (The biggest impact is that users cannot yet fully personalize their experience. Although the prototype demonstrates how users might select apps, contacts, and focus durations, these selections do not produce real changes in the system.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
525 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 928 0 R
/E (The statistics provide an example of how progress could be displayed, but users cannot evaluate how accurately the product would track their own behavior.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
526 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 929 0 R
/E (The absence of the physical duck also limits our ability to evaluate the emotional connection between users and the duck, which is a central part of our design.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
527 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 318 0 R
/E (Overall, these limitations mean that our prototype is better suited for evaluating navigation, interface clarity, and the overall concept than for testing real-world functionality, personalization, or long-term engagement. However, we believe it still provides a useful foundation for gathering feedback and identifying improvements before implementation.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
